-- title:
--   Membership in the three-torsion set
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group, $N=|G|$, $H=G[2]=\{u:2u=0\}$, $h=|H|$, $t=|G[3]|$, and $D=|2G|$. Write $R_S(z)$ for the ordered pair-sum count of a finite support $S$, $F(S)=\{T:|T|=3,R_T=R_S\}$, $O(S)=\{S+u:u\in H\}$, and $F^*=\{S\in F:0\notin S\}$. Ordinary full fibres have size $h$, exceptional full fibres size $2h$. All displayed subtractions are natural subtraction, truncated at zero, and all quotients are integer division. For any $v\in G$,
--
--   $$v\in G[3]\iff3v=0.$$
--
--   The zero element is included.
-- source:
